T*
(Soft-deprecating re.match\(\) Python has a concept of soft deprecation , where APIs are marked as) Tj
T*
("should no longer be used to write new code" without any promise/threat to remove them in the) Tj
T*
(future. Python 3.15 release manager Hugo van Kemenade describes how in the upcoming 3.15) Tj
T*
(release soft deprecation has come for the venerable but deeply confusing re.match\(\) function.) Tj
T*
(It's now available with the much clearer alternative re.prefixmatch\(\) name - reflecting how it) Tj
T*
(anchors at the beginning of the string but not the end. Most of the time you probably want) Tj
T*
(re.search\(\) \(match this pattern anywhere in the string\) or re.fullmatch\(\) \(match the entire) Tj
T*
(string\) instead. Via Lobste.rs Tags: python , regular-expressions) Tj
