(4. ?Apple Reference Image: A New Approach for Verified Photography?) Tj
T*
(Source: Daring Fireball | Published: 2026-09-16T02:38:24Z) Tj
T*
(Link: https://security.apple.com/blog/apple-reference-image/) Tj
T*
(Apple Security Research has released a concise, cogent paper describing how Apple Reference) Tj
T*
(Image works, and why they made it. A terrific read. Here?s just one fascinating bit regarding) Tj
T*
(privacy: Other industry solutions require a photographer or institution to vouch for an image) Tj
T*
(using their own credentials. We are concerned this puts some photographers, such as those) Tj
T*
(operating in conflict zones, in a difficult position; it should not be necessary to forgo) Tj
T*
(anonymity in order to prove image authenticity. We built Apple Reference Image to avoid using) Tj
T*
(an explicit, public credential for photographers, and to avoid even implicit public association) Tj
T*
(between different photos taken by the same sensor. The final reference image is instead signed) Tj
T*
(by Apple?s signing service, after validation by PCC. That signature is backed by Apple?s) Tj
T*
(strongest technical guarantees. Our implementation also protects the confidentiality of the) Tj
T*
(image itself, including from Apple. Merely capturing a reference image should never expose the) Tj
T*
(actual pixels to Apple or anyone else. We achieve this through the exceptional privacy) Tj
T*
(properties of PCC ? the nodes themselves are architected so that not even Apple can access...) Tj
T*
() Tj
