T*
(Source: Andrew Nesbitt | Published: 2026-09-15T09:00:00+00:00) Tj
T*
(Link: https://nesbitt.io/2026/09/15/shadowing-the-standard-library.html) Tj
T*
(I was reading Johann Rehberger?s write-up of an attack on a coding agent last week. The payload) Tj
T*
(is a file called struct.py inside a zip archive. The agent unpacks the archive, writes its own) Tj
T*
(small Python decoder in the extracted directory, and runs it. The decoder does import base64 ,) Tj
T*
(base64 internally does import struct , and Python resolves that to the attacker?s file because) Tj
T*
(the script?s directory is the first entry on sys.path . Module-level code runs on import. The) Tj
T*
(poisoned module re-exports the real _struct API so decoding still produces valid output and) Tj
T*
(execution continues, and the payload relaunches itself with python3 -I so the second) Tj
T*
(interpreter starts with a clean module path. That -I is the tell that this is a well-understood) Tj
T*
(Python behaviour. Putting an ambient directory on the module search path is a default most) Tj
T*
(dynamic-language runtimes shipped with early on, and several have since removed it, so I went) Tj
T*
(through the ones I could find to see where each ended up. The problem is specific to resolving) Tj
T*
(module lookups at run time against filesystem locations, so languages that bind everything at) Tj
T*
(build time are mostly absent. Removed Ruby dropped . from $LOAD_PATH in 1.9.2...) Tj
T*
() Tj
