(13. Bottlenecks Get a Bad Rap) Tj
T*
(Source: Jim Nielsen?s Blog | Published: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:00:00 GMT) Tj
T*
(Link: https://blog.jim-nielsen.com/2026/bottlenecks/) Tj
T*
(Poor bottlenecks. Always seen as problematic, antithetical to efficiency. But bottlenecks) Tj
T*
(aren?t universally bad. Think about it: a bottle?s neck is designed to constrain the amount of) Tj
T*
(liquid that can flow out. A decrease in bandwidth is its entire purpose! Otherwise an) Tj
T*
(overwhelming amount of liquid flows out and makes a big mess. We humans have a particular) Tj
T*
(anatomy. We can only consume so much liquid at a time. The neck of a bottle works with that) Tj
T*
(fact. We could make machines to produce so much wine that we?re drowning in it. But that) Tj
T*
(wouldn?t change the fact that we?re only capable of consuming so much liquid at a time \(not to) Tj
T*
(mention digestion , etc.\). When it comes to liquid consumption, the bottle?s neck isn?t the) Tj
